{"primitive": "noul", "context": "Glucose syrup containing over 90% glucose is used in industrial fermentation, but syrups used in confectionery contain varying amounts of glucose, maltose and higher oligosaccharides, depending on the grade, and can typically contain 10% to 43% glucose. Glucose syrup is used in foods to sweeten, soften texture and add volume. By converting some of the glucose in corn syrup into fructose (using an enzymatic process), a sweeter product, high fructose corn syrup can be produced.", "question": "Is the answer to this question yes: is glucose syrup the same as high fructose corn syrup?", "choices": ["true", "false"], "ordered": false, "answer": 1, "source": "boolq", "id": "boolq-4939"}
